  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize the central pool. If there is only one card of a rank in the pool, and you have that card, take it immediately! This ensures you don't 'Lie Down' for at least one more turn. Don't play pairs from your hand unless forcedâ€”save them as insurance.\n\nPair Hoarding: If you have a pair in your hand, don't play it immediately. Save it as a 'buffer.' If your turn comes and no table capture is possible, you can play one of your pair cards to take the other from the table in the next turn (assuming it survives). Watch for opponents' mistakesâ€”be ready to claim uncollected pairs or mournivals.\n\nTable Clearing: If you are the leader, try to leave the pool as 'rank-depleted' as possible. If you take the only 7 on the table, the next player who holds a 7 is much more likely to be forced to 'Lie Down.' Force opponents to use their pair cards early by threatening to capture the table cards they need.",
    Player: "Prioritize the central pool. If there is only one card of a rank in the pool, and you have that card, take it immediately! This ensures you don't 'Lie Down' for at least one more turn. Don't play pairs from your hand unless forcedâ€”save them as insurance.\n\nPair Hoarding: If you have a pair in your hand, don't play it immediately. Save it as a 'buffer.' If your turn comes and no table capture is possible, you can play one of your pair cards to take the other from the table in the next turn (assuming it survives). Watch for opponents' mistakesâ€”be ready to claim uncollected pairs or mournivals.\n\nTable Clearing: If you are the leader, try to leave the pool as 'rank-depleted' as possible. If you take the only 7 on the table, the next player who holds a 7 is much more likely to be forced to 'Lie Down.' Force opponents to use their pair cards early by threatening to capture the table cards they need.",
